1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,500
That drip under your tailpipe—

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,000
normal, or worth worrying about?

3
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:05,000
On a cold Cleveland morning,

4
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:07,000
water dripping from your exhaust is common.

5
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:09,500
Burning fuel creates water vapor.

6
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:13,000
In a cool muffler, it condenses and drips out as your engine warms up.

7
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:16,000
But sweet-smelling white smoke that keeps going after warm-up

8
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:19,000
can point to a coolant leak into the engine.

9
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,500
One clue is not a diagnosis—

10
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:25,000
worth checking your coolant level early, before it becomes a bigger repair.

11
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Stop by and we'll take a look—

12
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Nick's Tire and Auto, on Euclid Avenue.

13
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,000
